/**
 * Abbreviates a String by truncating it to a maximum length, preferring to break at a word boundary.
 * The abbreviation process considers a 'lower' bound as the starting point for searching for a word break,
 * and an 'upper' bound as the maximum length for the prefix of the string before any suffix is added.
 * If the string is longer than the specified 'upper' limit, it will be truncated, and the
 * {@code appendToEnd} string will be added.
 *
 * <p>The method operates as follows:</p>
 * <ol>
 *   <li>If the input string is {@code null}, {@code null} is returned.</li>
 *   <li>If the input string is empty, an empty string is returned.</li>
 *   <li>The {@code lower} parameter is normalized to be non-negative. It defines the minimum index
 *       from which to start searching for a space character to use as a word break.</li>
 *   <li>The {@code upper} parameter is normalized to be non-negative (unless -1, which means no limit).
 *       It defines the maximum length of the string's prefix before {@code appendToEnd} is added.</li>
 *   <li>If {@code upper} is -1 or greater than the string's length, it is adjusted to the string's length.</li>
 *   <li>If {@code upper} is less than {@code lower}, {@code upper} is adjusted to be equal to {@code lower}.
 *       This ensures that the maximum prefix length is at least the starting point for word search.</li>
 *   <li>If the original string's length is already less than or equal to the effective {@code upper} limit,
 *       the original string is returned as no abbreviation is needed.</li>
 *   <li>Otherwise (if the string is longer than {@code upper}), the string is abbreviated:
 *     <ul>
 *       <li>It searches for the first space character starting from the {@code lower} index.</li>
 *       <li>If a space is found at or before the {@code upper} limit, the string is truncated at that space.</li>
 *       <li>If no space is found within the relevant range (from {@code lower} up to {@code upper}),
 *           the string is truncated strictly at the {@code upper} character limit.</li>
 *       <li>The {@code appendToEnd} string is then appended to the truncated prefix.</li>
 *     </ul>
 *   </li>
 * </ol>
 *
 * <p>Example usage:</p>
 * <pre>
 * WordUtils.abbreviate("This is a long sentence", 5, 10, "...")  = "This is..."
 * WordUtils.abbreviate("VeryLongWord", 0, 7, "...")             = "VeryLon..."
 * WordUtils.abbreviate("Short", 0, 10, "...")                   = "Short"
 * WordUtils.abbreviate("Another example", 10, 12, "...")        = "Another..."
 * WordUtils.abbreviate("Hello World", 0, 5, "...")              = "Hello..."
 * WordUtils.abbreviate("Hello World", 6, 8, "...")              = "Hello Wo..."
 * </pre>
 *
 * @param str         the String to abbreviate, may be null.
 * @param lower       the minimum index from which to start searching for a word break. Must be non-negative.
